@startuml components
title RetroAgent - Component diagram

skinparam componentStyle uml2
left to right direction

actor "User" as User

cloud "Model service" as ModelService {
  component "Hosted or local model" as Model
}

node "User machine" {

  package "retroagent" {

    component "CLI" as CLI

    package "Runtime" as RuntimePkg {
      component "Session" as Session
      component "Turn loop" as Turn
      component "Cycle command" as Cycle
      component "Permissions and approvals" as Permissions
      component "Slash commands" as Commands
    }

    component "Context builder" as Context
    component "Provider adapter" as Provider
    component "MCP client" as McpClient

    package "Bundled MCP servers" as Servers {
      component "git server" as GitServer
      component "memory server" as MemoryServer
      component "test_runner server" as RunnerServer
      component "reports server" as ReportsServer
    }

    component "Data layer" as DataLayer
    component "Metrics and decision" as Metrics
    component "Report renderer" as Renderer
    component "Configuration" as Config

    folder "resources" as Resources {
      artifact "steering" as Steering
      artifact "skills" as Skills
      artifact "templates" as Templates
      artifact "examples" as Examples
    }

    interface "ModelProvider" as IModelProvider
    interface "MCP over stdio" as IMcp
    interface "Memory API" as IMemory
  }

  database "Project memory" as Database
  folder "Target project" as Target {
    artifact "git repository" as Repo
    artifact "RETRO.md" as RetroMd
    artifact "run evidence" as Evidence
    artifact "generated tests" as GeneratedTests
    artifact "reports" as ReportFiles
  }
  folder "User configuration" as UserConfig {
    artifact "config.yaml" as UserYaml
    artifact "approvals.json" as Approvals
  }
  node "Worktree" as Worktree {
    component "Test command" as TestCommand
    component "Service under test" as Service
  }
}

User --> CLI : commands and messages
CLI --> Session : starts
Session --> Config : reads
Session --> Turn
Session --> Commands
Commands --> Cycle
Cycle --> Turn : one turn per step
Turn --> Permissions : checks every tool call
Turn --> Context : builds context
Turn ..> IModelProvider : calls
Provider -up- IModelProvider
Provider --> Model : HTTPS or local HTTP
Turn --> McpClient : dispatches tool calls
Commands --> McpClient : direct commands
McpClient ..> IMcp
GitServer -up- IMcp
MemoryServer -up- IMcp
RunnerServer -up- IMcp
ReportsServer -up- IMcp

Context --> Steering : loads
Context --> Skills : loads
Context --> RetroMd : reads
Context ..> IMemory : state digest
Session ..> IMemory : session record, tool calls
Permissions --> Approvals : reads and writes
Config --> UserYaml : reads

DataLayer -up- IMemory
GitServer ..> IMemory
MemoryServer ..> IMemory
RunnerServer ..> IMemory
ReportsServer ..> IMemory
DataLayer --> Database : SQLite, invariants

GitServer --> Repo : reads
RunnerServer --> Worktree : creates, runs, removes
RunnerServer --> Evidence : writes JUnit XML and logs
RunnerServer --> GeneratedTests : writes and copies
TestCommand --> Service : HTTP
ReportsServer --> Metrics : evaluates
ReportsServer --> Renderer : renders
Metrics ..> IMemory : reads records
Renderer --> Templates : fills
Renderer --> ReportFiles : writes Markdown, SVG and PDF
CLI --> Examples : retro example

note right of Permissions
  Enforced before dispatch:
  modes, permissions and the
  approval of project commands.
end note

note bottom of DataLayer
  Only writer of the database.
  No tool accepts a test result:
  results come from parsed JUnit XML.
end note

note bottom of Provider
  The only component that
  talks to a model.
end note

@enduml
